{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914494540},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. using two data sources:\n1. https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv (farmers markets data)\n2. https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv (census/population data)\n\nAccording to the project instructions, I need to:\n1. Orient first by checking semantic models and catalog aliases\n2. Only ingest sources if no existing alias covers the data\n3. Use xorq_select to compute values\n4. Declare obligations and verify with xorq_verify\n5. Check lineage with xorq_check_lineage\n\nLet me start by checking if there's a catalog already set up and if there are any semantic models or aliases that might cover this data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by orienting with the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NBEcpqpAcrg813WgXEknyz","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GF7ikUh1a55iRm5QWGCoi3","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":376,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8153,"totalTokens":8539,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0018800000000000002,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01019125,"total":0.012081250000000002},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":233},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914494551,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77PL7BoJ7m3H4Hbpkqj","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01NBEcpqpAcrg813WgXEknyz","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914499270},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01GF7ikUh1a55iRm5QWGCoi3","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914499270},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both data sources. According to the instructions, I should:\n1. Write build scripts under `.xorq/scripts/`\n2. Use xo.deferred_read_csv to read the sources\n3. Build the scripts and add them to the catalog\n\nFor this task, I need to:\n1. Ingest farmers markets data and get the total count\n2. Ingest census/population data and get the total U.S. population\n3. Create a derived metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me start by creating build scripts for each source.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"No existing aliases, so I need to ingest both sources. Let me create build scripts and add them to the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01RR9FtotHACT8aRs35q1i4f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01YXm5q9A1Ne5ahYiGSN5eTR","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py","content":"import xorq as xo\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"})\n)\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011fN6uuqUDHFKKY5gQSJ3Az","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/census_population.py","content":"import xorq as xo\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"})\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":562,"cacheRead":8153,"cacheWrite":473,"totalTokens":9202,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0028100000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0008153,"cacheWrite":0.00059125,"total":0.0042305500000000005},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":145},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914499270,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77PgBBHrEYt4Q6L7SH5","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01RR9FtotHACT8aRs35q1i4f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914503975},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01YXm5q9A1Ne5ahYiGSN5eTR","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 245 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914503975},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_011fN6uuqUDHFKKY5gQSJ3Az","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 284 bytes to .xorq/scripts/census_population.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914503975},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to build these scripts and add them to the catalog. I'll use the xorq build command for each.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014KtAgyfreYst3612ypopKY","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-17-ee0s1926 && xorq build .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_fm.txt && cat /tmp/bp_fm.txt"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01PmNNuhHBdvDwTArxfZdo1H","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-17-ee0s1926 && xorq build .xorq/scripts/census_population.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp_cp.txt && cat /tmp/bp_cp.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":261,"cacheRead":8626,"cacheWrite":692,"totalTokens":9593,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0013050000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0008626,"cacheWrite":0.000865,"total":0.0030466},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":31},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914503975,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77Pzrq83Y4wxWGc3gJh","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014KtAgyfreYst3612ypopKY","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Building expr from .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 797, in invoke\n    return super().invoke(ctx)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 1873, in invoke\n    return _process_result(sub_ctx.command.invoke(sub_ctx))\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 1269, in invoke\n    return ctx.invoke(self.callback, **ctx.params)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/click/core.py\", line 824, in invoke\n    return callback(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/cli.py\", line 1149